		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A class expression is never a huggable argument: prettier's `couldExpandArg` has no",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 106
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " class arm, so a member call breaks a sole class argument onto its own line exactly as",
			"start": 108,
			"end": 196
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " a plain call does.",
			"start": 198,
			"end": 219
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " Member call, chained call, a longer chain, optional call, and a chain on a `new` head",
			"start": 222,
			"end": 310
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " With a heritage clause, an `implements` clause, a decorator and a comment-only body,",
			"start": 522,
			"end": 609
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " and through `as` / `satisfies` / `<T>` / `!`",
